<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roermond</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Roermond is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> province of Limburg, where the Roer joins the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a>. A chief town of the Duchy of Guelders, it became the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-guelders">Upper Guelders</a> and the seat of a bishopric in 1559, and it stayed with the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt">Dutch Revolt</a>. Its Munsterkerk and cathedral date from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roermond.jpg" alt="Roermond" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Grundig · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hochwasser_auf_Maas_und_Rur_in_Roermond.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
